    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!--
        carddemo-tests — CONSUMER-MOST module of the multi-module build graph
        and the NON-NEGOTIABLE quality gate for the Java 25 LTS CardDemo
        implementation (AAP §0.3.6, §0.6.11).

        Contents (per AAP §0.2.1, §0.3.1, §0.6.11):
          * Golden-record harness — one *GoldenTest.java per COBOL program
            from app/cbl/*.cbl, asserting byte-for-byte parity between Java
            output and captured COBOL output. Test sources live under
            src/test/java/com/blitzy/carddemo/tests/golden/. Captured COBOL
            outputs live under src/test/resources/golden/&lt;program&gt;/expected/.
          * jqwik property-based tests — DecimalsProperties.java in
            src/test/java/com/blitzy/carddemo/tests/property/ achieves the
            100% line coverage on monetary code mandated by AAP §0.6.1 and
            §0.7.2 by generating random BigDecimal inputs in COBOL-valid
            ranges and asserting Java/COBOL agreement on add/subtract/
            multiply/divide/round operations with MathContext.DECIMAL128 and
            the COBOL-mandated RoundingMode (HALF_EVEN for ROUNDED, DOWN for
            default truncation).
          * JFR-based performance regression tests — JfrBaseline.java in
            src/test/java/com/blitzy/carddemo/tests/perf/ captures Java Flight
            Recorder recordings of representative batch runs and asserts no
            performance regression beyond a 10% band per AAP §0.6.11 and
            §0.7.2. JFR recordings are written under
            ${jfr.recording.dir} == ${project.build.directory}/jfr.

        Reads the 9 ASCII fixtures in ../app/data/ASCII/ via classpath relative
        path (NOT COPIED into this module per AAP §0.4.1 and §0.6.11).

        Architectural rule (AAP §0.3.6):
          * This is the CONSUMER-MOST module — it depends on carddemo-app
            (the composition root) and transitively on every other internal
            module (carddemo-batch, carddemo-application, carddemo-adapter-file,
            carddemo-adapter-db, carddemo-domain).
          * NO module depends on carddemo-tests — never the reverse.
          * This is a JAR-packaged module with NO src/main/ — all code lives
            in src/test/. This is a valid Maven idiom for a test-only module.
          * The harness exercises the FULLY-ASSEMBLED system end-to-end,
            instantiating carddemo-app main classes (PostTransactionsApp,
            InterestCalculationApp, etc.) and running them against the 9
            ASCII fixtures from ../app/data/ASCII/.

        Forbidden in this module (AAP §0.1.1 architectural override, §0.6.7,
        §0.6.12, §0.7.4, and the file's "Forbidden in this Module" list):
          * Spring / Spring Boot Test / Spring Test / Spring Data / Spring
            Batch Test / Spring Security Test / Spring MVC Test / Spring
            Cloud AWS — NO Spring container exists in this refactor per AAP
            §0.6.12, so there is nothing to test for Spring wiring.
          * Mockito-Spring (mockito-spring) — no Spring context to mock.
          * Mockito (in general) by default — Java 25 records and sealed types
            enable plain test doubles without bytecode rewriting; if Mockito
            is ever added later it must be justified in MIGRATION_NOTES.md.
          * Testcontainers (org.testcontainers:*) — AAP §0.5.1 explicit
            exclusion; file-based fixtures are the default.
          * LocalStack (cloud.localstack.*) — AAP §0.5.1 explicit exclusion.
          * Hibernate / JPA / jakarta.persistence — no Hibernate in this
            project.
          * Lombok — Java 25 records replace it.
          * Flyway / Liquibase — no DB migration in this project (AAP §0.6.12).
          * Micrometer / Prometheus / Grafana / Jaeger / OpenTelemetry —
            JFR-only observability per AAP §0.6.12.
          * PowerMock — Java 25 + records + sealed types make it
            unnecessary and incompatible.
          * H2 / HSQLDB embedded databases — file-based testing only.
          * PostgreSQL / MySQL / DB2 JDBC drivers at test scope — AAP default
            is file-based batch (AAP §0.7.5).
          * The "enable-preview" JVM flag (the double-dash variant) in any
            compiler/surefire configuration (AAP §0.6.7, §0.7.4 — only
            finalized JEPs are permitted: JEP 506 ScopedValue, JEP 510 KDF,
            JEP 511 Module
            Import, JEP 513 Flexible Constructor Bodies, JEP 519 Compact
            Headers, JEP 521 Generational Shenandoah).
          * &lt;source&gt;/&lt;target&gt; tags — the parent POM's
            &lt;release&gt;25&lt;/release&gt; is the single source of truth
            for the Java language level.
          * double / float for any monetary assertion — use BigDecimal with
            explicit scale and RoundingMode (AAP §0.6.1, §0.7.4).
          * ThreadLocal in any test fixture or helper — use ScopedValue
            (JEP 506 Final) per AAP §0.6.6, §0.6.7.

        Runs on every PR per AAP §0.6.11. Test failures here BLOCK MERGES.
    -->

    <parent>
        <groupId>com.blitzy.carddemo</groupId>
        <artifactId>carddemo-parent</artifactId>
        <version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>carddemo-tests</artifactId>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <name>CardDemo Tests (Golden-Record Harness, Property Tests, JFR Baselines)</name>
    <description>
        Non-negotiable quality-gate test harness for the Java 25 LTS CardDemo
        implementation. Contains: (1) byte-for-byte golden-record parity tests
        (one *GoldenTest.java per COBOL program from app/cbl/), (2) jqwik
        property-based tests achieving 100% line coverage on the Decimals
        utility per AAP §0.6.1 and §0.7.2, (3) JFR-based performance
        regression assertions within a 10% band per AAP §0.6.11. Runs on
        every PR per AAP §0.6.11. Reads ASCII fixtures from app/data/ASCII/
        via classpath relative path (NOT copied per AAP §0.4.1).
        Depends on carddemo-app (composition root) which transitively brings
        in carddemo-batch, carddemo-application, carddemo-adapter-file,
        carddemo-adapter-db, and carddemo-domain. NO Spring, NO Testcontainers,
        NO LocalStack, NO --enable-preview per AAP §0.6.7, §0.6.12, §0.7.4.
    </description>

